    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.26) headlining the lineup, as both benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and a manageable matchup against McClanahan. While both carry a 36% rain risk, their ceiling remains the highest in our daily projection model. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) remains a pillar of consistency today, even against a tough lefty in Weathers, as his elite base contact profile and advantageous order placement solidify his spot as our premier 1B option. We are closely monitoring the weather in that contest; should a rainout occur, our bench depth will be tested immediately, though we have no healthy reserves currently rostered who provide the same offensive output as these starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup today involved **Heliot Ramos** (45.34) and the choice to keep him in the outfield over the marginal options on our bench. **Heliot Ramos** was nearly bumped in favor of a more aggressive defensive posture, but his positive adjustment due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014providing a tactical edge for our stolen base priority\u2014tipped the scales. Elsewhere, **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) provides a strong, balanced profile, though his score was tempered slightly by the need to balance his high stolen base potential against the risk of hitting against a tough pitcher. We are avoiding exposure to our injured reserves like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung**, leaving us reliant on **Miguel Vargas** (47.82) to provide utility value. While we have depth options like **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White** on the secondary squad, none currently offer a better projected path to point production than our active starters.\n\nBeyond the rain threat for **Liam Hicks**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Coby Mayo**, we are proceeding with caution against Cease, who presents a hurdle for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**. We have prioritized speed today, as **Nasim Nunez** (45.85) remains in the lineup specifically for his ability to swipe bags, despite his lower overall efficiency score. We will be tracking the efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** at the top of the order; his matchup against Henderson is less than ideal from a skill perspective, but his leadoff role is essential for maximizing our total plate appearances in a tight 5x5 race.",
